<!-- From -->
From Ubiq on the <a class=post href=http://boards.stratics.com/cgi-bin/forum/origin/postlist.pl?Cat=&Board=uo2devboard&page=1&view=expanded&sb=5>Stratics DevBoard</a>:
<!-- End From -->
<!-- Begin Story -->
<!-- Indent --><table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" border="0"><tr><td width="15"><img src="/images/blank.gif" width=15 height=1 border=0 alt=""></td><td><font face="Arial" size="-1" color="#000068"><!-- End Indent-->
ORIGIN has a paper doll. It shows the character from the front, and it animates with whatever your real character is doing at the time. Next to the paper doll are some tabs that bring up his bio, what he's wearing and other things.
<p>
You don't need the paper doll to dress your character - you can just drag your stuff onto your 3D representation in the world. But you need it to undress your character. This will hopefully help take some of the pain out of removing teensy items, like rings and necklaces.
<p>
Ubiq
<!-- /Indent --></font></td></tr></table><!-- End /Indent -->
