			<td><table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" bgcolor="White">
		<tr>
			<td width="100%" bgcolor="#E0DEC5"><font color="black" size="-1" face="arial">&nbsp;<b>The Success of the UO World Faire</b></font></td>
		</tr>
		</table></td>
		</tr>
		</table>
			<font face="Arial" size="-1" color="Black">
<!-- From -->
From Ubiq on the <a class=post href=http://boards.stratics.com/cgi-bin/forum/origin/postlist.pl?Cat=&Board=uo2devboard&page=0&view=expanded&sb=5>Stratics DevBoard</a>:
<!-- End From -->
<!-- Begin Story -->
<!-- Indent --><table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" border="0"><tr><td width="15"><img src="/images/blank.gif" width=15 height=1 border=0 alt=""></td><td><font face="Arial" size="-1" color="#000068"><!-- End Indent-->
Depends on how you define success.<br><br><br>* Did we get good feedback from the fans about our products?   We got awesome feedback, some of which will undoubtedly be incorporated into both products.<br>* Did we have a successful unveiling of UO3D?  I think so, the buzz about it has been very good. <br>* Did the people who came feel like they got their money's worth?  Judging from the feedback we got, it seems that most of them did.<br>* Did we make money?  We did okay.  Not a lot, but that was never really as important as the other goals anyway.<br>* Did the Origin team need an excuse to stop working and go and drink together?  Most assuredly yes.<br><br>So by that measure, I guess that it was a success!<br><br>Probably our greatest feedback was that people wished that the faire could have been held elsewhere (most frequently in their own hometown =).  Granted, <br>we may have gotten a greater turnout if we had held it in a big city like LA or NY, but it would have had other negatives.  For one thing, convention halls are pricier there.  For another, the fact that the event was in Austin meant that the MAJORITY of both the UO and the ORIGIN teams were able to attend.  If it had been elsewhere, that would likely have been unfeasible.<br><br>Ubiq
<!-- /Indent --></font></td></tr></table><!-- End /Indent -->
<!-- End Story -->
<!-- Thanks -->
Thanks!
<!-- End Thanks -->
</font>


