From Gaffer on the <a class=post href=http://boards.xrgaming.net/forums/list.php?f=96>CoNB DevBoard</a>:
<!-- End From -->
<!-- Begin Story -->
<!-- Indent --><table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" border="0"><tr><td width="15"><img src="/images/blank.gif" width=15 height=1 border=0 alt=""></td><td><font face="Arial" size="-1" color="#000068"><!-- End Indent-->
You'll see a more diversity of looks of characters in general from the screenshots coming out now (well, OK, that last one is a guy in full head-to-toe pneumatic armor, if I recall right, but in general:)  Or ask for folks who saw the video to comment...there are a ton of different looks in there (Jukan with a mohawk in a trenchcoat, anyone?).
<BR>
<BR>In earlier months, it took a lot of work for us to customize people (you'd have to use GM/art tools, create items, etc.) - so most of the guys in the videos went with "stock" characters.  Now more of the character creation is in place, and so different hairstyles, skin/hair colors, etc. are more easily attainable, so you see more variation in the videos/screenshots.  It's a simple answer, I know, but go figure.  Oh, also, a lot more clothing/armor art is in, so you'll see more of that too.  
<BR>
<BR>Coordinating 10-12 people to be in the video is a tremendous pain ("OK, now everyone log into the crystal forest, and change your characters, no, too many Jukans, and you two are wearing the same outfit, and...")- it's why we do 'em so rarely.  At least now showing gameplay is easier; drop a bunch of monsters in the game and go fight 'em while someone moves their camera near.  One tricky bit was that we had to have healers standing off camera nearby casting healing spells on the monsters and warriors to keep em from dying during combat all the time - we don't have an "don't die" cheat flag yet :)
<BR>
<BR>-jg
