			<font face="Arial" size="-1" color="Black">
<!-- From -->
From Gaffer on the <a class=post href=http://boards.xrgaming.net/forums/list.php?f=96>CoNB DevBoard</a>:
<!-- End From -->
<!-- Begin Story -->
<!-- Indent --><table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" border="0"><tr><td width="15"><img src="/images/blank.gif" width=15 height=1 border=0 alt=""></td><td><font face="Arial" size="-1" color="#000068"><!-- End Indent-->
The combat system math is way too extensive to be posted all in a lump; Damion and Ben have generally been pretty good about releasing internal details of math though, so over time we'll probably talk about it a fair bit unless there's a really strong reason not to.
<BR>
<BR>Why's the math intensive?  Because while the basic "I have this much bonus to hit, this much to damage" kind of bit is easy, the items you have affect this a lot in different ways based on what piece of your armor gets hit, how it was crafted, what enchantments are on it (and you), what damage absorbtion the armor has, what skill boxes you and your attacker have, etc.  It's a couple of pretty big docs, since it covers everything from skills to attributes to items to crafting - it'd be very tough to get into combat math without hitting tons of other systems.
<BR>
<BR>Also, we're still tweaking enough stuff (Mobius did a very cool system, but all things change a bit during implementation as you see it working, get to balance, etc.) that what we released now probably wouldn't resemble exactly what you'll see at beta/launch, and it'd be confusing to have multiple docs out on it (IMO).
<BR>
<BR>Having said all that, as things get finalized we shouldn't have a problem talking about the math - y'all are generally damn good at poking holes in things, and we'd always rather find out issues before we go live where possible.
<BR>
<BR>-jg
<!-- /Indent --></font></td></tr></table><!-- End /Indent -->
<!-- End Story -->
<!-- Thanks -->
Thanks!
<!-- End Thanks -->
</font>


